# Pre-code design pass

Do not start implementation on a security-sensitive change until this is written and internally coherent. Then wait for adversarial review (Architect) before coding, unless the user said "quick fix, no loop."

Print:

```text
SECURITY INVARIANT:
PROTECTED ASSET:
TRUST BOUNDARY: (trusted / untrusted)
ATTACKER:
ATTACK PATH:
ENFORCEMENT POINT:
SUPPORTED MODEL:
NON-GOALS:
FAILURE SEMANTICS: (every uncertainty fail-closed/open)
STATE / LIFECYCLE: (if any)
FAILURE CLASSES:
MINIMAL DESIGN:
COMPLEXITY BUDGET:
RED TESTS: (positive, negative, race, stale, restart, bypass as needed)
WHAT I WILL NOT BUILD:
```

Then: RED on the vulnerable baseline → smallest fix → GREEN → focused tests → race if concurrent → `go test ./...` → harness/lint → independent review.

Never claim "tests pass" without exact SHA, exact commands, and the property those tests prove.
